  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Departures Board",
    "overview": "Every court is a row, every free time is the next departure, and your own game is the only thing lit amber. The app is a quiet neutral shell (office-grey in light, board-black in dark) around black board panels that stay black in both themes. Inside a panel, type is condensed and tabular, rows are separated by 1px seams rather than shadows, and times are split-flap tiles that flip when the value changes. Outside a panel, it is ordinary web UI: Barlow, sentence case, standard controls at 44px.\n\nThe mood is sporty and energetic in the details (the flap, the lamp, condensed numerals) and calm in the task: booking never competes with decoration. Members see only free, taken and yours, readable without a legend. The office reads the same grammar as dense tables with status lamps. The system refuses the startup look: no gradients, glass, glow or soft halos, and no white cards with pastel time chips.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Black board panels (board-frame) in both themes; neutral true-grey ground around them (chroma 0).",
      "One lamp: amber means yours, the primary action, or live. It is never decoration and never a data series for counts.",
      "State is a word plus a mark (check, dash, dashed outline, lamp dot), never color alone.",
      "Hairline seams (flap-seam) and 1px rings instead of shadows; floating layers alone carry a soft shadow.",
      "Two faces: Barlow Condensed for the board voice, Barlow for everything readable."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Lamp Rule",
        "body": "Amber marks yours, the primary action, or live state and nothing else. Disabled primary is a neutral fill with muted ink, never dim amber.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lamp Ink Rule",
        "body": "On light grounds amber text, links, rings and chart marks use amber-ink; the bright amber is for fills with #111111 ink and for black surfaces.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Board Stays Black Rule",
        "body": "Board panels are #1a1b1b with #0e0f0f faces in both themes; only the shell around them changes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Board Voice Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase condensed lives on the board: board titles, court names, column headers, flap text and the primary booking button. Page titles, nav, card headings, buttons and body stay sentence case. No eyebrows or kickers.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Seam Rule",
        "body": "Inside a board, separation is a 1px seam. Shadows belong to things that float above the page.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Focus Rule",
        "body": "Focus is a 2px outline in the ring color (amber-ink on light, amber on dark and on boards) with a 2px offset (1px on text fields), everywhere.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep board panels #1a1b1b with #0e0f0f faces and #2a2c2b seams in both themes.",
      "Do use amber only for yours, the primary action and live state, and amber-ink (#a35c00) for amber text, links and focus on light grounds.",
      "Do pair every state with a word or mark: check for yours, dash for occupied, dashed empty cell for not available, dot plus text for payment.",
      "Do keep 44px targets, 16px body and 2px amber focus outlines with a 2px offset.",
      "Do flip times as split-flap characters when the value changes, and honor reduced motion with the 120ms crossfade.",
      "Do keep condensed uppercase to the board (titles, court names, column headers, flap text, the booking CTA) and sentence case elsewhere."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use gradients, glass, glow, soft focus halos or startup-style decoration.",
      "Don't add a blue lamp or color a neutral count series amber, green or red.",
      "Don't show \"not available\" as a dash; the dash means occupied.",
